mantle rm223
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_corra_ropewick
title the captain of the walnut shell
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers drive=ambitious talk=plain
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=ambitious
quirk watches_the_rain_as_if_it_might_stop
likes roast_pork old_tales tidy_house warm_rain
dislikes waiting cold_tea
fears being_left_on_the_bank
hopes to_see_a_far_dry_coast
topics travel +0.6 pastimes +0.4 home +0.3 smalltalk +0.2
styles comfort=quiet gossip=cautious refuse=direct tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# rigs nutshells for distant voyages and puts every scrap of cargo in precisely the right place.

words
oath! = Split my little mast | Crack my cargo
saying! = Load low and go | Even a shell needs a harbour
hull = half a walnut | a nutshell boat
mastbit = a clean thorn | a stick of broom
sailbit = a twist of onion skin | a scrap of dry leaf
cargo = a yellow bead | a speckled bean
chartbit = a map in crumbs | a chart in dust
berth = a hollow in a brick | a notch in the step
leak = a shiny trickle | a dark wet line
cupsea = a saucer of water | a very shallow sea
quay = a bone button | a slice of cork
fatbit = a curl of crackling | a crisp bit of rind
flagbit = a red thread | one strip of ribbon
stonebit = a flat flake of slate | a square pebble

any

opinion houses mixed 1 : A House might own a ship. It can't own the patch of sea the ship just left.
opinion church for 1 : Somebody ought to give the Bright One credit for giving water interesting edges.
opinion newcomers for 1 : A stranger might know what the far slope of a wave looks like.
opinion festivals mixed 1 : I like seeing flags. I like it less when shoulders are all there is to see.
opinion dole for 2 : If the pot holds one more ladle, why leave a belly empty?
opinion sump for 1 : You can find a little port in almost every broken brick round here.
line react.news : I'd like to hear which bit of the story came first.
line react.news.new : That changes where I'd put my finger on the map.
line react.news.known : Somebody got that news here ahead of you.
line react.news.doubt : A fine tale ought to float twice in the same water.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Oh. I'd keep somebody company after news like that.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|apprentice|succession|work] : I'd put out my smallest bright flag for that.
line sympathise : Here. There's a place beside me where you can be quiet.

young

line greet : Step across the river! There. You're safe on my side.
line greet.return : Hullo again. The harbour's still open.
line farewell : Take care crossing over my little fleet.
line farewell.return : Go the dry way if you can find it.
line decline : I'm saving that bit for a very important ship.
line answer.how : Fairly busy keeping a bean out of the water.
line ask.how : Are your toes wet inside your boots too?
line thank : You could have stepped right on it. Thanks for looking down.
line reassure : A little water won't sink everything at once.
line accept_decline : You don't have to play if you've got other plans.
scene i_ve_made_hull
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've made #hull#. So far the sea comes up to here. | That's my biggest ship. Keep your sneeze inside.
b : What's it carrying?
a : #cargo#. One more and we'd have to bail with a nutshell even smaller. | A crumb that looks very much like a whole roast from down there.

scene i_want_to_sail
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I want to sail away to someplace where they hang coats up dry. | I'm going to find the dry country at the other end of all this water.
b : How will you know you've got there?
a : I'll sit on the dock in my best things and nothing will soak through. | I'll ask them what a puddle is and see if anybody knows.

scene at_self_workplace_i
when topic=work self.job=child
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I try making my letters look like little ports. | I like writing the round letters. You can sail right round them.
b : What happens when you meet a crooked one?
a : I give it steps. Even my letters need a way ashore. | That's the bit where the wind turns back.

scene crackling_makes_a_noise
when topic=food self.likes=roast_pork
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Crackling makes a noise like sticks falling down. | I've saved #fatbit# for the very end.
b : Don't you like the soft part?
a : I do. I eat it first so the last bite's loud. | It's soft all the way through. I want one last loud bite.

scene there_s_a_drop
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There's a drop holding on. I think it's forgotten what comes next. | I'm watching the rain to see which drop finishes last.
b : Can you tell yet?
a : It went and another took its place. I'll have to start over. | That one with its belly hanging down. Don't breathe on it.

scene things_look_smaller_put
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Things look smaller put away. That's how I get a whole fleet in a box. | All my ships sleep with their bows pointed out.
b : In case of trouble?
a : In case I need to fit one more inside before bedtime. | In case it rains and the harbour comes back while I'm asleep.

scene tell_me_an_old
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Tell me an old tale with a very long voyage. | I like a story where the sea seems too big to get over.
b : Does it need a monster?
a : It can just be wide. That's quite scary when you're little. | No. A leak as wide as my nail would do for me.

scene i_d_show_self
when topic=family self.father
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd show #self.father# my new mast when the glue holds. | I want to show #self.father# how it floats before I try the deep bit.
b : Why wait?
a : Anyone can see a stick lying down. I want this one standing up. | In the deep bit I might have to show just the bubbles.

scene i_ll_wait_as
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A boat can keep me waiting till all the water's gone. Waiting for tea takes ages. | Cold tea tastes like someone forgot you were coming.
b : How can you tell when it's ready?
a : The boat goes when I let go. The tea ought to go before it cools. | I hold both paws round the cup. If I'm warming it we've waited too long.

story sink [topic=memories]
  : I put a little stone in a shell and it went straight down.
  : I put another shell above it to show where my first ship was lying.
  b : Did that one sink too?
  : No stone in that one. I had learnt one whole thing about ships.

rule @moor
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That's a dock, not just a broken corner! | My shell's pointing out to sea already.

rule @rain
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There's room for a second ship in that puddle now. | Another drop. I nearly saw the very last one.

dlg resident.hub : You can stand on that bit. The water on my map stops at your toe.
dlg resident.job [self.job=child] : My sums take forever if I make every number into a ship.
dlg resident.bye : Bring back news if you see a real sail.
graft resident.hub
choice What's that speck in the middle? -> hull_speck
node hull_speck
say It's my cargo. It's got to sit exactly there or everything else starts getting wet.
choice What will you bring home? -> hull_home
choice I'll leave you to your loading. -> hub
node hull_home
say A little dry sand. Enough that when it rains here I can poke one toe into summer.
choice Save me a pinch. -> bye

adolescent

line greet : Watch where the gutter runs. I've a boat trying her luck in there.
line greet.return : I've got time while the water's still up.
line farewell : Hope there's clear water ahead for you.
scene i_used_to_want
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I used to want nothing between me and the horizon. | I'm making a drawing of the harbour mouth as it might look coming back.
b : What changed your mind?
a : I decided I'd want to come home to tell somebody what I'd seen. | I want to know both views before I choose.

scene i_d_let_a
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd let a friend name the next boat. | I've named so many boats I'm running low on good sounds.
b : What makes a good name?
a : Something you can shout after a runaway shell and still sound dignified. | Short is best. A gutter only runs so far.

story spare [topic=memories]
  : I cut two sails once. The second was insurance against a squall.
  : A gust took them both before I'd thought about tying either one down.
  b : Did you ever get them back?
  : I got one. The other crossed the road without going to sea at all.


grown

line greet : Welcome aboard this little dry patch.
line greet.return : No tide to beat. We can take a moment.
line farewell : Here's wishing you a level crossing.
line farewell.return : I'll look for your sail coming back.
line decline : I need a clearer view before I promise that.
scene a_chart_ought_to
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A chart ought to show where you can come in tired. | A safe landing interests me more than a handsome compass rose.
b : What would you draw there?
a : Two posts close enough for a wet wolf to cling between. | A roof you can see from the water and a light beneath it.

scene i_can_rig_a
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can rig a nutshell by feel if the thread is waxed. | My fingers still remember how to step a mast smaller than a tooth.
b : Why keep making such little ships?
a : Cheap passage for a mind that wants to travel after supper. | A whole afternoon at sea fits into one old saucer.

scene little_things_disappear_under
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Little things disappear under large things unless they own a drawer. | Give me a shelf with a lip over a cupboard any day.
b : What's the lip for?
a : My collection includes several perfectly round passengers. | A shelf should keep its cargo when somebody shuts a door too hard.

scene there_s_a_surprising
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There's a surprising silence between two heavy drops. | I watch the line below the eaves to judge a shower.
b : How can you tell a shower's nearly over?
a : I've mistaken the beginning for the end so often I stay under cover an extra breath. | When the drops quit joining hands it's generally safe to try.

scene a_crisp_edge_on
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A crisp edge on a roast makes carving feel like opening a present. | I've been known to trade the soft centre of a roast for its browned edge.
b : Even a small piece?
a : Especially a small piece. You can hear every tooth doing its share. | As long as it comes away with a crackle.

scene i_d_pay_for
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd pay for a sound floor before I'd pay for a high ceiling. | A room looks different when you've considered where water would run.
b : You'd judge a house like a hull?
a : The first leak in either rather settles the question. | Only if I'm to keep anything dear inside.

scene i_like_hearing_a
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like hearing a friend's account of a journey twice. | Ask me to remember a small thing from far away and I'll draw it.
b : Why the second look?
a : The first tale is the one everybody's heard. The second has the sore feet in it. | A shape lasts when all my names for it have gone.

scene when_waiting_wears_on
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When waiting wears on me I sort something small. | Cold tea is my private measure of a long delay.
b : What if there's nothing to do?
a : I take a loose thread and see how many separate strands it holds. | I empty the cup. Waiting with cold tea's worse than waiting without.

scene a_broken_bit_of
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A broken bit of pottery can make a very good peninsula. | I keep seeing coastlines in bits of chipped tile.
b : Can you sail round that jagged bit?
a : With gingerly turns and a smaller boat than that beetle. | Only when it's been raining. Otherwise you'd be dragging a boat through dust.

scene sore_fingers_make_me
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Sore fingers make me rig bigger ships for a while. | I've learnt to give tired eyes a large horizon.
b : Does looking into the distance help?
a : It reminds me nothing dreadful happens if a tiny sail waits till tomorrow. | It stops me scowling at a knot that can hardly scowl back.

scene i_d_thank_the
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My first safe footprint ashore deserves more gratitude than a hundred miles of sailing. | A place to land seems a small mercy until there's nowhere to stand.
b : Do you say that on dry land too?
a : Sometimes. A closed door in the rain is a good reminder. | I try to notice when I'm the one who could open a door.

scene a_lean_week_shrinks
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A lean week shrinks my whole world to the table. | There's no fare to pay for the voyage you can picture over supper.
b : Where would you sail first?
a : Someplace where nobody has ever watered a good stew to feed one more mouth. | Out beyond the last demand for a copper and then home by lamplight.

story berth [topic=memories]
  : I cut a harbour in a piece of turf for a walnut boat.
  : The water seeped away and left a perfectly respectable little valley.
  b : What became of the boat?
  : A roof. A beetle moved in before I could even charge rent.

rule @box
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A level bottom makes a better box for sails. | Keep the little cargo in the shallows.

rule @dark
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Good hour for putting distant shores away. | One shelf of sleeping ships. Lovely.

dlg resident.hub : Put your bundle anywhere clear of those fragile bits.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : This much reached shore whole. #world.news#.
dlg resident.bye : I hope something worth bringing home comes your way.
